Spec: Place search

Purpose:
  Find a place by name from the map view of the History tab and set the area pin there, so "rides around
    here" does not need a long press on the right spot.

Owns:
  ./*.dart
  ./widgets/*.dart
  /test/place_search

References:
  /lib/features/history_map/history_map.sdd
  /lib/domain/area_filter.sdd
  /lib/map/map.sdd

Can modify:
  /lib/features/history_map/history_map_view.dart
  /lib/features/history_map/widgets/map_controls.dart
  /docs/play-store.md
  /docs/app-store.md

Must:
  The map view shows one magnifier button among its controls (the Komoot map has the same). It opens a search
    field over the map; closing it brings the controls back. The suggestions scroll inside the room the map
    leaves above the attribution, so the source line stays in view over the keyboard. The magnifier in the History header stays what it
    is: it searches the rider's rides by title, in the list and on the map alike.
  Typing asks Photon (`https://photon.komoot.io/api`, OpenStreetMap data, no key) for places. A request goes out
    only after the rider paused typing for `400` ms and the text has at least `3` characters; an older request
    is dropped when a newer one starts. At most `5` suggestions show, each with its name and a second line with
    the city and country.
  The request carries the typed text, the app language (`lang`, `de` or `en`) and the app's user agent of
    @Map (Photon refuses the default one) and nothing else: no position, no ride data, no identifier. Photon's fair-use rules are kept: no request per keystroke, no bulk use.
  Choosing a suggestion sets the pin there like a long press: the pin keeps a radius chosen before (default
    `5` km), the camera moves to it once and shows the whole circle, and the search field closes.
  An empty result says so ("no place found"); a failed request (offline, error, timeout of `8` s) says the search
    is not available now. Both leave the map and the pin as they are.
  Opening the search closes an open ride preview card, and no card shows while the search is open (#108).
  Queries and results are not stored on the device or logged.
  The search panel names its source: "Search by Photon · © OpenStreetMap".
  The privacy policy on getretrail.app (repo `retrailWeb`) and the store data-safety answers say that the typed
    search text goes to Photon (photon.komoot.io) when the rider uses the place search, and nothing is sent
    otherwise.

Must not:
  Take more than `100` characters in the field.
  Send text while the field is empty, under `3` characters or unchanged since the last request.
  Send the rider's position, ride titles, filters or any identifier.
  Replace or hide the ride search of the History header.

Scenario: find a place
  Given the map view is open without a pin
  When the rider taps the magnifier, types `Hamb` and picks "Hamburg, Germany"
  Then the pin is set in Hamburg with a radius of `5` km, the camera shows the whole circle and the field closes

Scenario: typing pauses
  Given the search field is open
  When the rider types `Hamburg` letter by letter within `400` ms each
  Then one request goes out, with the full text, after the last letter

Scenario: a ride preview is open
  Given a ride's preview card is open on the map
  When the rider taps the magnifier
  Then the card is gone and the search field is open

Scenario: too short
  Given the search field is open
  When the rider types `Ha`
  Then no request goes out and no hint about failure shows

Scenario: no network
  Given the device is offline
  When the rider types `Hamburg`
  Then the panel says the search is not available now and the map is unchanged

Scenario: the ride search stays
  Given the History header search holds `loop`
  When the rider opens the place search
  Then the ride filter `loop` stays on the list and the map

Example:
  Request: `https://photon.komoot.io/api/?q=Hamburg&limit=5&lang=de`
  Suggestion line one: `Hamburg`, line two: `Hamburg, Deutschland`

Tasks:
  [x] #106 Photon client behind a provider (debounce, drop older requests, parse name and place line).
  [x] #106 Magnifier button and search panel over the map; choosing a suggestion sets the pin.
  [x] #106 German and English copy, glossary entry, source line.
  [x] #106 Store data-safety answers; the privacy policy text is an issue in `retrailWeb`.
  [x] #106 Device check: typing on a phone, offline, pin and camera after choosing (Pixel 7, 2026-11-12).

Done when:
  Every Scenario passes as a test, the policy and store answers name Photon, and the device check is done.
